text:
Quality score: 6.5/10. The project is small, readable, and has a passing test suite, but I would not approve it as-is because several uncovered cases can corrupt or misreport accounting data.

Verification: `pytest -q` passed with 61 tests. `compileall` could not complete because the workspace is read-only for `__pycache__` creation.

```json
{
  "score": 6.5,
  "issues": [
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "70-81",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Older equal-rank records can overwrite newer RUNNING or terminal job data because freshness is not compared."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "74-80",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Rows are treated as unchanged when only state, end, and elapsed_sec match, so corrected CPU/GPU/user/partition/exit_code values are silently ignored."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "129-134",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Unknown or typoed states are accepted without validation, then later treated as terminal lifecycle states."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "40-41",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Unrecognized states default to terminal rank, which can block legitimate later active-state updates."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "107-114",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Negative GPU counts in AllocTRES are accepted and can produce negative GPU-hours."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "148-162",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Negative AllocCPUS values are accepted and can produce negative CPU-hours."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/reports.py",
      "lines": "14, 65, 115-121",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Timestamp filtering and newest-time selection use lexicographic text comparisons, which are wrong for offset-aware datetimes."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "152-163",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "Blank User, Partition, and ExitCode fields are accepted, causing reports to group jobs under empty labels."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/cli.py",
      "lines": "121-126, 138-143, 172-180",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "Report commands create a new empty database on a missing or mistyped --db path instead of warning the operator."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/reports.py",
      "lines": "50-70, 74-110, 124-152",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "Report queries have no supporting indexes for reference time, state, user, or partition, so scans will become expensive as history grows."
    },
    {
      "file": "tests/test_ingest.py",
      "lines": "21-70",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Ingest tests do not cover same-rank out-of-order updates or corrected resource fields, leaving the main data-corruption paths untested."
    }
  ],
  "lines_to_rewrite": 180,
  "approve": false
}
```
